boss fights are almost becoming a relic  of the past with fewer and fewer games  featuring big bads but they're not gone  and forgotten yet this year had a few  awesome standout boss fights that  challenged you in new ways including the  final boss of wolfenstein which offered  up a nice surprise throwback for fans of  the series as well as the bevy of  tactics and planning that you'd have  needed to gather up in order to take out  the numerous bosses of transistor but  here are my five picks for best boss  fights of 2014.  a boss fight isn't necessarily good  because the boss is particularly hard or  that it has a sweet design it needs to  offer you something more than that  like i don't know for example respawning  all the major bosses of a region for an  all-out assault early on in divinity  original sin before your party is beefy  as [ __ ] you need to face off against  brachus rex that on its own would be  dealable but he's brought along the  poison laced ghoul that guards the  lighthouse the fiery twins by fire  joined and diederich the sword wielding  baron of bones they've all got lists of  strengths and vulnerabilities as long as  they're names so you need to be careful  about which attacks to use when and  where and try not to get hemmed in by  the lot of them on the plus side this  difficult level 9 fight prepares you  extremely well for the rest of the game  by demanding a mastery of the elemental  system by teaching you that fire  explodes poison oil costs slow and so on  destiny might seem like a contentious  choice but its first raid vault of glass  is surprisingly engaging the six-player  raid consists of three stages opening  the vault offing the templar and  launching an assault on the glass throne  in order to kill atheon the final boss  easy right no  not easy the raid is filled with a bunch  of game mechanics that were nowhere to  be seen in the main game new enemy types  puzzles to solve and an instance where  your party gets separated at random none  of this is ever explained and the first  group to finish the raid allegedly took  over 8 hours to work it out like any  good boss fight the vaulted glass is  particularly clever in the way that it  forces you to adapt and learn new  situations and really work as a team in  order to come out alive  it probably comes as no surprise that  being at a 2 is filled with epic bosses  the batshit crazy game is just  overflowing with larger-than-life foes  but here's some of the best even though  you'll probably just be using your  tried-and-true combos and witch-time  tactics to take out well everybody the  design and scope of these baddies is  insane there's towering infernal dragon  creatures who dwarf your leggy  protagonist mighty and well-equipped  angels as well as speedy enormous  spiders each fight ends in a unique  climax finishing move which really  cements its status as over the top it's  difficult to say whether bayonetta 2's  bosses are lovely or ludicrous in this  regard but whichever way you look at the  plethora of gargantuan villains they  certainly belong on this list  shovel knight is another game that is  just packed with awesome bosses but none  are more tough or fun than the final  boss the enchantress the awesome thing  about the face-off between shovel knight  and the enchantress is that you aren't  alone at this point in the game you've  rescued your beloved shield knight after  countless trials and he or she fights by  your side and acts as a necessary part  of this battle a feature that solidifies  how essential she is to your protagonist  in the narrative it's a tricky set of  three stages that involve dodging  fireballs and jumping off shield  knight's shield to get to higher ground  the battle is also incredibly worth it  for the payoff an unexpectedly touching  final sequence  finally and inevitably we have dark  souls 2 the champion series of badass  bosses whose lives are dedicated to  messing you up and they do repeatedly  there are loads of worthy adversaries in  the souls series and dark souls 2  delivered some awesome ones the pursuer  who you may be incredibly unlucky to  encounter early on does his very best to  chop you up into tiny little pieces with  his adept sword and shield skills the  incredibly unfair ruined sentinels will  have you throwing your controller across  the room if you don't bring along some  friends and then there's the smelter  demon for a lot of people he's the worst  of the lot with devastating and quick  blows from his flaming sword one of the  very coolest though has to be the  executioner's chariot a roaring  horse-drawn chariot that tries to bowl  you over your only respite from the  red-eyed shadow horses are to hide in  small alcoves until you can work out  what to do as with everything in dark  souls you can't hide forever  that is it for my picks be sure to let  me know which video game battle of 2014  was your favorite and i'll catch you  again next week
 

